<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Rhine Gorge, Caumasee and Conn loop — Staderas–Caumasee–Conn / Il Spir–Staderas [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From the actual Staderas walking trailhead, follow the forest approach by Prau la Selva and the real path junctions to the outer Caumasee walking shore. Continue along the marked lake and forest tracks to Conn, visit Il Spir by its complete out-and-back walking spur, then return through the forest to the same Staderas trailhead.

Normally April–November outside snow and ice, with current signs, restrictions and weather governing passage. Follow the marked forest paths and viewing facilities, keep away from gorge edges and respect cyclists on shared ground. Wear suitable walking shoes and carry weather protection, drinking water and a route map. Mapped bridges and viewing structures are not a current safety inspection.

Lake and swimming-facility entry is paid and subject to current admission rules. The outer walking course does not grant entry to that facility. Check parking, transport, lift and restaurant schedules separately; no fee amount, free admission or operating service is promised.

Protect the lake, forest and wildlife habitats, stay on the marked course and avoid trampling vegetation or disturbing animals. Nearby Uaul Grond wildlife quiet-zone restrictions apply December 20–May 31 with passage only on indicated routes; this walking line does not intersect the captured zone. Follow current local notices rather than extending that result to all surrounding ground.

Approximately 9.5 km, independently rounded from the complete mapped course. The 282 m ascent, 282 m descent and 180-minute duration remain approximate legacy planning estimates, without surveyed heights or an elevation profile. This two-dimensional line is for planning, not navigation or an assurance of safety.

